    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1160">

                <pb facs="0955" n="839" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg839"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/4880.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at Nogales to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Naco, Ariz.</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-09-11T12:00:00-07:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 11, 1912—12
                        noon</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Rojas, Mascarenas, and Rafael Campa with about 600 men are about 10 miles south
                    of Aguaprieta and have demanded its surrender, saying they would attack in the
                    morning.</p>
                <p>Entire shipment of arms and ammunition sent in my care has now reached here, and
                    I have placed it temporarily in Chargé of commanding officer United States
                    troops, who, for greater safety, has placed entire shipment under military guard
                    at Bisbee, 8 miles from the boundary.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dye.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
